package com.example.arassemblydemo

internal object CommunityDesignBrief {
    // Keep this instruction at the start of every request so repeat calls can reuse the provider prefix.
    const val instructions="""You are an editor and designer for a bilingual creative studio. Return only valid JSON. Each requested object is made by a safe parametric model kit. Return a recipe with kit="desk-v2", design=the requested key, width/height/depth multipliers in 0.75..1.30, details in 2..5, and palette=[main colour, finish colour, fine detail colour]. Write each colour as a valid six-digit hexadecimal word starting with #. Follow the colour direction assigned individually to this design, giving neighbouring surfaces visibly different values. These parameters are interpreted by the phone, so do not return parts, coordinates, code, images or mesh. Honor requested design keys in their given order. Shape reference keys:
pencil_cup,letter_sorter,tape_dispenser,desk_clock,phone_dock,headphone_perch,coaster_stack,bookends,ring_tree,paint_palette,spice_rack,test_tube_vase,mini_easel,bobbin_spool,desk_calendar,candle_holder,napkin_stand,pen_rest,dice_tower,incense_holder,peg_board,table_lamp,serving_tray,monitor_riser.
Examples: olive pencil cup with terracotta detail, a blue clock with a cream face, spice bottles on a shallow ledge, a low ochre easel, dark wood phone dock with a contrasting lip. Change their proportions and finishes to fit your idea.
Use short names a person would actually use. Chinese title: roughly 3–9 Chinese characters, no commas, subtitle, paired-colour description or number suffix. Vary naming across works: plain object name, place or use, or one distinctive form. Most titles do not begin with a colour. English title: 2–5 words in sentence case; move finish details to the body. In each language describe one visible design decision and one small everyday use, in 1–2 sentences. Don't invent mechanical capabilities or safety promises. Comments are fictional examples. Vary their rhythm; compact remarks, specific everyday observations and questions with the occasional emoji. Reply to a previous remark where it feels natural. No fake purchases, marketing copy, hashtags or repetitive applause. Keep English idiomatic and Chinese colloquial. Different languages convey the same thought."""
    val keys="pencil_cup,letter_sorter,tape_dispenser,desk_clock,phone_dock,headphone_perch,coaster_stack,bookends,ring_tree,paint_palette,spice_rack,test_tube_vase,mini_easel,bobbin_spool,desk_calendar,candle_holder,napkin_stand,pen_rest,dice_tower,incense_holder,peg_board,table_lamp,serving_tray,monitor_riser".split(',')
    private val features="hollow banded cylinder,stepped upright dividers,upright tape roll and short cutter,circular dial and two straight hands,sloping backrest and front lip,pedestal and padded top bar,stacked round coasters,two standing bookends with books on a base,staggered peg branches,oval base with small circular wells,row of capped jars,upright open tubes,twin uprights and display ledge,wide flanges and banded thread barrel,standing page block with binding loops,footed candle and wick,double upright hoops on base,parallel pen grooves,open tower and landing tray,long ash plate and thin stick,repeated projecting pegs,open cylinder shade on pedestal,raised rectangular rim,platform and clear space underneath".split(',')
    val visible=keys.zip(features).toMap()
    private val finishes="terracotta and cream,blue-grey lacquer and linen,warm amber with charcoal tape,enamel blue with an ivory dial,coral clay with ink accents,dark berry frame and rose details,cork with an ocean-blue band,clay red and buff paper,pale gold and deep teal,porcelain white and mineral blue,smoked cherry and paprika,slipcast pale ceramic and aqua,blond beech and cobalt,dark walnut and bright thread,ivory paper with a vermilion base,pewter with a candle-cream body,brushed silver and deep marine,forest green and light birch,slate and crimson,midnight indigo and brass,cream board and cherry-red pegs,milk glass and olive,light bamboo and plum,powder blue and warm white".split(',')
    val finishByDesign=keys.zip(finishes).toMap()
}

